t_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-326355","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001365135","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1365135/000119312526326355/wu-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/cd6d95729cd50b041bd66f6611a1d9059de862a56405974d3bc7c5ca93064a4b.bin","sha256":"cd6d95729cd50b041bd66f6611a1d9059de862a56405974d3bc7c5ca93064a4b"}},{"id":"541ae01ae3a9ccd1abd609127f59e9da804fe73dc08c404bb842c09049599a17","quote":"The Company’s CODM is the President and Chief Executive Officer. The CODM uses segment operating income or loss to assess performance, including by comparing the results of each segment with one another, and allocate resources to the segments. This measure includes all expenses necessary to operate the segment and enables the CODM to understand segment profitability based on prior resource allocation decisions. This measure also excludes certain expenses such as exit costs and other severance which may be driven by corporate initiatives or could result in a lack of comparability if included in segment operating income.","context":"As further described in Note 1, the Company has classified its business into the following segments: Consumer Money Transfer and Consumer Services. Operating segments are defined as components of an enterprise that engage in business activities, about which separate financial information is available that is evaluated regularly by the Company’s Chief Operating Decision Maker (“CODM”) in allocating resources and assessing performance.","section":"14. Segments","block":351,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-326355","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001365135","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1365135/000119312526326355/wu-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/cd6d95729cd50b041bd66f6611a1d9059de862a56405974d3bc7c5ca93064a4b.bin","sha256":"cd6d95729cd50b041bd66f6611a1d9059de862a56405974d3bc7c5ca93064a4b"}},{"id":"46ffe0f3b39519cfee91220be1ebcbe784dfdad96809577ae1254ac0ff562203","quote":"The Consumer Money Transfer operating segment facilitates money transfers between two consumers. The segment includes five geographic regions whose functions are primarily related to generating, managing, and maintaining agent relationships and localized marketing activities. The Company includes Branded Digital transactions in its regions. By means of common processes and systems, these regions, including Branded Digital, create one interconnected global network for consumer transactions, thereby constituting one Consumer Money Transfer business and one operating segment.","context":"The Company’s CODM is the President and Chief Executive Officer. The CODM uses segment operating income or loss to assess performance, including by comparing the results of each segment with one another, and allocate resources to the segments. This measure includes all expenses necessary to operate the segment and enables the CODM to understand segment profitability based on prior resource allocation decisions. This measure also excludes certain expenses such as exit costs and other severance which may be driven by corporate initiatives or could result in a lack of comparability if included in segment operating income.","section":"14. Segments","block":352,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-326355","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001365135","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1365135/000119312526326355/wu-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/cd6d95729cd50b041bd66f6611a1d9059de862a56405974d3bc7c5ca93064a4b.bin","sha256":"cd6d95729cd50b041bd66f6611a1d9059de862a56405974d3bc7c5ca93064a4b"}},{"id":"13ca30a53cd63c4e7e69702729a9ed93d44e1ed45b8e544db274c86ff475a0a7","quote":"The Consumer Services segment primarily includes the Company’s bill payment services, money order services, travel money services, check acceptance services, media network, prepaid cards, lending partnerships, and digital wallets.","context":"The Consumer Money Transfer operating segment facilitates money transfers between two consumers. The segment includes five geographic regions whose functions are primarily related to generating, managing, and maintaining agent relationships and localized marketing activities. The Company includes Branded Digital transactions in its regions. By means of common processes and systems, these regions, including Branded Digital, create one interconnected global network for consumer transactions, thereby constituting one Consumer Money Transfer business and one operating segment.","section":"14. Segments","block":353,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-326355","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-07-30","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001365135","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1365135/000119312526326355/wu-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/cd6d95729cd50b041bd66f6611a1d9059de862a56405974d3bc7c5ca93064a4b.bin","sha256":"cd6d95729cd50b041bd66f6611a1d9059de862a56405974d3bc7c5ca93064a4b"}},{"id":"c8e3534a68bdcbb85bd946a21ecfb5c67723b2b3f34acc9f696001925daf836f","quote":"The Company’s segments are reviewed separately below because each segment addresses a different combination of customer groups, distribution networks, and services offered. The business segment measurements provided to, and evaluated by, the Company’s CODM are computed in accordance with the following principles:","context":"The Consumer Services segment primarily includes the Company’s bill payment services, money order services, travel money services, check acceptance services, media network, prepaid cards, lending partnerships, and digital 